.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt CHKPASSWD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm chkpasswd
.Nd check a user's password
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl i Ar infosystem
.Op Fl l Ar location
.Op Ar name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
asks for the password of
.Ar name ,
or of the user who runs it, and checks it.
If the password is wrong, it prints
.Dq Sorry .
With the file, NIS and opendirectory systems it then exits with status 1.
With PAM, the default, it exits with status 0 whatever the result.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c
Compare the password as typed, without encrypting it first.
This applies to the file and NIS systems.
.It Fl i Ar infosystem
Check the password with
.Ar infosystem ,
one of:
.Bl -tag -width opendirectory
.It Cm file
the password file
.It Cm nis
NIS
.It Cm opendirectory
the directory service
.It Cm PAM
the
.Pa /etc/pam.d/chkpasswd
policy
.El
.Pp
The default is
.Cm PAM .
.It Fl l Ar location
For
.Cm file ,
the password file, by default
.Pa /etc/master.passwd .
For
.Cm nis ,
the NIS domain.
For
.Cm opendirectory ,
the directory node, such as
.Pa /Local/Default .
Without it, the authentication search node is used.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/pam.d/chkpasswd -compact
.It Pa /etc/pam.d/chkpasswd
the PAM policy
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr pam_opendirectory 8
